decide('204640 204641 204642 204643 204646 204647 204648 204649 204650 204651 204686','Likely covered','Bundled realm enables eventsEnabled, adminEventsEnabled and detailed admin events. Keycloak user/admin records identify time, action, realm/resource and actor/source/outcome; UDS alternative adds an explicit JSON stdout listener. Forwarding/notification settings are evaluated separately.','realm core-id-audit')
decide('204645','Likely covered','Keycloak has login/admin event logging enabled, and API JWT/permission gates provide the authentication/authorization path. Verify the final event selection against required transaction types, but logging capability and enabled events are established in source.','realm authz app-enforcer')
decide('204656','Likely covered','Bundled Keycloak configuration enables the realm, disables registration/username edits/reset and implicit flow, and uses a minimal dedicated service image; UDS provides an explicit flow/feature configuration. Extra product modules need a release inventory, not a presumption of a missing hardening mechanism.','realm core-keycloak')
decide('204659','Likely covered','Keycloak is exposed through the tenant gateway with ambient mesh enrollment, and default-deny/declared ports constrain access. The final PPSM/network profile remains a documented deployment input.','core-network mesh identity')
decide('204660 263531','Likely covered','Keycloak/OIDC assigns individual identities and API binds validated subject to tenant/user context; this supplies individual identification before shared application resource access. Service credentials are not treated as human group logins.','realm authz')
decide('204661 204662','Needs work','The bundled candidate defines local user login and no CAC/PIV/X509/MFA authentication flow. Core has the X509/OTP implementation, but selecting bundled identity does not consume it automatically.','identity realm core-keycloak','Select UDS/federated CAC identity or configure the bundled authentication flow/trust; validate privileged and ordinary paths.','pki-authentication',category='configuration/integration')
decide('204670','Needs work','Neither bundled passwordPolicy nor the pinned UDS default includes an eight-character difference constraint. Password history/length do not enforce the exact change-distance requirement.','realm core-id-realm','Provide an enforcing provider policy/custom validator or accepted rule-specific directory/applicability disposition.','identity-policy',category='configuration/tailoring')
decide('204675 204676 204678','Needs work','The chosen bundled realm contains no X509 authentication flow or mapping/revocation configuration. UDS identity-config has X509 identity mapping and OCSP support, but those are not activated for the bundled candidate.','identity realm core-keycloak core-id-realm','Configure the selected CAC/X509 path, approved trust anchors, user mapping and fail-closed revocation behavior; UDS-mode inheritance is an alternative implementation.','pki-authentication',category='configuration/integration')
decide('204677','Likely covered','Keycloak/gateway private material is supplied using Kubernetes Secret mounts/references and platform namespace controls; client CAC private keys remain on the credential device rather than being delivered in the application image.','core-gateway app-pods')
decide('204680 204681','Likely covered','No automatic account deletion/inactivity-disable policy exists in the bundled candidate; it therefore does not automatically remove/disable emergency accounts. An emergency-account designation and access policy still needs documentation.','realm identity')
decide('204682 204683 204684 204685 204687','Needs work','Bundled realm enables stored admin events but has no event-to-SА/ISSO notification route. UDS\'s optional logging alert templates monitor its own platform realm and do not automatically attach to the bundled realm.','realm core-id-notify','Forward bundled identity admin events and configure notification receivers, or use the approved UDS identity integration.','audit-alert-routing',category='configuration/integration')
decide('204690','Needs work','The bundled realm enables stored events but defines no eventsListeners JSON/stdout forwarding listener. Vector collects stdout, not Keycloak\'s internal database event store; therefore the source does not establish centralized authentication-event delivery. UDS identity-config implements the needed listener for its own realm.','realm core-id-audit core-vector','Enable a suitable event listener/forwarder for bundled Keycloak or consume the UDS identity service.','identity-audit-forwarding',category='configuration')
decide('204699','Unclear','The candidate generates a bootstrap admin credential and individual local users, but source does not identify who holds that admin account or whether it is a shared operational login. Code cannot establish actual human account ownership.','identity app-namespace','Record named administrator accounts and restrict bootstrap/break-glass credential use; verify no shared human logins.',category='account ownership')
decide('204700 204702','Needs N/A justification','These network/device-management AAA checks do not describe the selected OIDC web-application identity role. The official check conditions applicability on device/privileged network management; document the component boundary rather than inventing VLAN configuration inside Keycloak.','identity core-network','Confirm the selected AAA service does not manage network devices/802.1x access; retain accepted component-specific rationale.',category='applicability')
decide('263532 263533 263534','Needs work','Bundled passwordPolicy contains hashing only and no blacklist/compromised-password check or update mechanism. The source therefore does not enforce a maintained compromised-password list for local passwords.','realm','Configure a maintained provider/blacklist integration for local accounts or accepted delegated provider control.','identity-policy',category='configuration/service')
decide('263535','Needs work','resetPasswordAllowed=false and the candidate supplies no operational recovery/required-password-change workflow. Disabling self-service reset is not evidence of forced change after administrator recovery.','realm','Implement/document required-action UPDATE_PASSWORD on account recovery or the selected provider\'s equivalent.','account-lifecycle',category='configuration/procedure')
decide('263536','Likely covered','The explicit Keycloak policy imposes hashing but no character-set/short maximum restriction; Keycloak supports user-supplied passwords/passphrases rather than application-side constrained password fields. Confirm any external provider limits when selected.','realm')
decide('263537','Needs work','No strength guidance/meter or configured password-selection validator is supplied for bundled local accounts beyond hashing. The required automated assistance is not delivered merely by enabling a password login form.','realm','Configure the selected provider\'s password-strength guidance/validation or use accepted delegated enforcement.','identity-policy',category='configuration')
decide('263538','Needs work','Bundled identity has no configured certificate-revocation cache. Even UDS identity-config defaults CRL checking off; OCSP alone does not establish the local-cache behavior this specific rule requires.','realm core-id-realm','Configure supported local CRL/cache refresh for disconnected operation or an accepted equivalent at the actual certificate-authentication boundary.','pki-trust',category='configuration/integration')


# PostgreSQL-specific semantics and defaults, checked against upstream primary docs.
def external_fact(key,url,text):
 b.E[key]=(key,text,url);FACTS[key]={'url':url,'observation':text,'kind':'primary upstream documentation'}
external_fact('pg-logging','https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-logging.html','PostgreSQL18 defaults connection logging disabled and disconnection logging off; failed authentication is always logged. stderr is the default server-log destination.')
external_fact('pgaudit-default','https://github.com/pgaudit/pgaudit/blob/REL_18_STABLE/README.md','pgAudit18 session audit classes default to none. Preload/CREATE EXTENSION alone does not enable READ/WRITE/ROLE/DDL auditing; log prefix supplies contextual identity fields.')
external_fact('pg-roles','https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/role-attributes.html','PostgreSQL role attributes govern LOGIN, privilege grants and connection limits; default per-role connection limit is unlimited. Superuser bypasses permission checks.')
external_fact('pg-password','https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-connection.html','PostgreSQL18 defaults password_encryption to SCRAM-SHA-256. Existing persistent data/configuration can override defaults; generated new credentials and selected image must be distinguished from existing volumes.')
external_fact('pg-encryption','https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/encryption-options.html','PostgreSQL supports password hashing and transport protection; volume/block encryption requires storage-layer configuration and is not established by creating a PVC.')
fact('core-flavors','uds-core',CORE,'docs/concepts/platform/flavors.mdx','Core distinguishes unicorn (curated FIPS-validated images), registry1 (Iron Bank hardening) and upstream (development/community images). The production hardened offering exists; actual selected flavor/digests and module mapping remain explicit deployment inputs.')
fact('app-jwt','horizon',b.H,'apps/api/src/api/auth/auth.oidc-jwt.service.ts','API uses jose jwtVerify with fixed issuer/audience/JWKS and expiry validation. It performs no online token introspection or logout/session revocation lookup; expected JWT failures are logged at debug level.')
fact('app-permission-table','horizon',b.H,'packages/database/schema/permission_audit.pg.hcl','Append-only role-grant/revocation table includes actor user, subject user, tenant, role, action and timestamp; it does not record every request or failed authorization.')

# Each database rule receives a DB-specific recommendation rather than web-SSO routing.
decide('206519','Needs work','Role creation grants LOGIN without CONNECTION LIMIT; PostgreSQL defaults that limit to unlimited. The official check supplies fallback limits when organizational limits are absent, so unspecified policy is not a reason to leave this unclassified.','app-db-role pg-roles','Set approved per-role concurrent-connection limits (including service-account/pool allowances) and verify the selected database configuration.','database-account-policy',category='configuration')
decide('206520','Unclear','The candidate deliberately uses DB-managed service/admin accounts. The official check permits them when documented and approved; code proves they exist but cannot prove the required organizational approval.','app-db-identity','Record approval/justification for each DB-native account and automation responsibilities; no mandatory SSO rewrite is inferred.',category='account approval')
decide('206521 206544 206547 206548 206552 206564 206571 206574 206585 206586 206587 206596 206597','Likely covered','PostgreSQL native roles/privilege checks and the separate horizon_app DML role restrict schema/administrative operations; non-root PGDATA isolation and UDS policy protect the process/files. SECURITY DEFINER functions are deliberate privileged modules and require an allow-list review, not a claim that PostgreSQL lacks access-control enforcement.','app-db-role pg-roles app-db-values core-policy')
decide('206522 206523 206527 206528 206530 206531 206532 206533 206534 206598 206616 206618 206620 206624 206626 206630 206632 206634 206635 206638','Needs work','Candidate config preloads pgaudit and creates its extension, but sets no audit classes, connection/disconnection logging or complete audit-context prefix. Upstream defaults do not generate the successful native DB activity/session trail this rule requires. Domain permission_audit rows are not a substitute for DBMS auditing.','app-db-values app-db-extensions pgaudit-default pg-logging app-permission-table','Define the approved event set, enable targeted pgaudit/native connection/context settings, forward to Loki and validate records plus performance/secret redaction. One audit configuration workstream covers these rules.','database-auditing',category='configuration')
decide('206525 206612 206636','Likely covered','The shipped/preloaded pgAudit extension can audit READ/ROLE/object operations using configurable classes, so audit-generation capability is present. Enabling the actual selected classes is separately flagged as database-auditing work.','app-db-values app-db-extensions pgaudit-default')
decide('206526 206613 206617 206619 206621 206625 206627 206631 206633 206637','Likely covered','PostgreSQL natively logs authentication and permission/error failures, while the standard server-log path is collected by Vector. This supports existence of failure events; full actor/source/content and successful-event coverage remain explicitly flagged under database-auditing.','pg-logging app-db-values core-vector')
decide('206529 206537 206594 206595','Likely covered','PostgreSQL server logging and timestamptz application audit fields use system time with subsecond precision; containers inherit MPN node time, and Vector preserves/labels the records.','pg-logging app-permission-table core-vector host')
decide('206538 206539 206540 206541 206542 206543','Likely covered','DB runtime runs non-root on a dedicated PGDATA PVC; audit settings are administrative PostgreSQL settings and ordinary application DML users cannot edit server config. Offloaded logs are isolated behind Loki/Grafana service/group controls. Review the separate bundled-Keycloak admin-credential gap as a privileged service residual.','app-db-role app-db-values pg-roles core-loki core-grafana')
decide('206545','Likely covered','DB installation/migration uses a separate administrative Secret and restricted job rather than application-user installer access; UDS/Kubernetes administration controls deployment changes. Document actual authorized administrators separately.','app-db-identity app-namespace core-policy')
decide('206546','Compliant','The database is in a dedicated container and PGDATA is a dedicated mounted persistent volume, separate from the node OS and other application containers. This is a source/configuration recommendation for the candidate filesystem layout.','app-db-values',category='source pass',owner='Gallatin SRE')
decide('206549 206550 206551','Likely covered','The custom Postgres runtime is assembled for the required PostGIS/pgvector/pgaudit functions and database migrations create the application/identity stores; the image does not ship a database sample application. Retain a final extension/database inventory to identify image-provided extras.','app-db-extensions app-db-values images')
decide('206553 206599','Likely covered','PostgreSQL has an internal ClusterIP service with declared application port5432 and no candidate public DB ingress; mesh/default-deny govern connectivity. Final approved PPSM/profile mapping remains required.','app-db-values core-network mesh')
decide('206554 206563','Likely covered','Separate application/admin/service credentials and native PostgreSQL role login identify processes; human application users are identified by OIDC and actor-aware domain audit. Non-organizational direct DB access is not enabled as an anonymous path.','app-db-identity app-db-role pg-roles authz app-permission-table')
decide('206555','Needs work','DB-native roles are created with passwords but no password-check hook, character/history/change-distance enforcement or VALID UNTIL lifetime policy is configured. Random initial credentials do not enforce future password changes, and PostgreSQL does not inherit Keycloak policy automatically.','app-db-role app-db-identity pg-roles','Define interactive/noninteractive account policy; configure enforcement or an accepted provider/credential-management control with the rule-specific exceptions.','database-account-policy',category='configuration')
decide('206556','Likely covered','The candidate uses PostgreSQL18 and CREATE/ALTER ROLE passwords without overriding password_encryption; upstream default stores SCRAM-SHA-256 representations. Inspect existing PGDATA hashes/settings before claiming the same for upgraded volumes.','app-db-role pg-password')
decide('206557 206567 206607 206608','Likely covered','Database clients and server are in the declared ambient mesh protected by root STRICT mTLS, so sslmode=disable is not proof of plaintext on the pod-to-pod wire. The approved FIPS module/trust-store claim is separate.','core-mtls mesh app-db-values')
decide('206558 206560 263617','Needs N/A justification','Selected PostgreSQL uses native password/service roles, not certificate-to-DB-user authentication. Mesh workload certificates protect transport and are not PostgreSQL PKI user mapping. Document the official PKI-based-authentication applicability boundary rather than configuring an unused DB certificate login.','app-db-identity mesh','Retain approved password-authentication/mesh architecture and rule-specific applicability; reassess if native DB PKI is introduced.',category='applicability')
decide('206559','Likely covered','Mesh/gateway private keys are managed in the platform Secret/identity boundary rather than world-readable database files; PostgreSQL native client private keys are not configured in the selected password-auth candidate.','core-mtls core-gateway app-db-values')
decide('206561','Likely covered','Native PostgreSQL password authentication does not echo a submitted password to the user, and the application log serializer redacts credentials. Avoid turning verbose SQL/audit parameter logging on without preserving that protection.','pg-password logging')
decide('206565 206566 206581','Likely covered','PostgreSQL server controls connection/backend session identifiers and terminates a connection/session on client disconnect; clients cannot preserve an authenticated DB session merely by replaying a browser-style session ID. The product provides native logout/connection close.','pg-roles pg-logging')
decide('206568 206606 206609','Likely covered','PostgreSQL supplies process-isolated backends, transactional/error semantics and authenticated connections; UDS restricts the container, and application input/error handling is explicit. Failed startup does not grant an authenticated SQL session.','pg-roles app-db-values app-error app-validation')
decide('206569','Needs work','PGDATA is persistent and logs are offloaded, but UDS Velero defaults disable volume snapshots and the candidate supplies no DB-aware backup/WAL/PITR/restore schedule. Persistence and resource-only backup do not establish recovery with least mission disruption.','app-db-values core-velero','Configure a database-consistent backup/recovery procedure and exercise restore; include SeaweedFS/PVC recovery scope.','data-backup-restore',category='configuration/operational validation')
decide('206572 206573','Likely covered','PostgreSQL role separation, application tenant/actor context and container process/PVC isolation constrain unintended data transfer. The final approved flow policy and security-label taxonomy are separate policy requirements.','app-db-role authz app-db-values core-network')
decide('206575 206576 206577','Likely covered','API input validation constrains declared inputs, and database migrations use format(%I/%L) for dynamic role identifiers/passwords instead of direct SQL interpolation in that provisioning path. PostgreSQL applies native SQL typing/privilege checks. A full arbitrary SQL vulnerability audit is not implied by this targeted mapping.','app-validation app-db-role pg-roles')
decide('206578 206579','Likely covered','Database errors presented to application users pass through the shared generic-error mapper; detailed diagnostics stay in restricted server logs. Direct administrative SQL sessions remain a privileged interface requiring approved role scoping.','app-error logging core-loki app-db-role')
decide('206580','Needs work','No idle_session_timeout/idle_in_transaction_session_timeout or role-specific session-termination policy is configured for native DB accounts in the candidate; Keycloak session timeouts do not terminate SQL connections.','app-db-values app-db-role','Configure role/account-type timeouts matching the approved disconnect policy and ensure pool/maintenance compatibility.','database-account-policy',category='configuration')
decide('206582 206583 206584 206614 206615 206622 206623 206628 206629','Unclear','These require organization-defined security/classification labels and associated access/audit behavior. Tenant IDs/domain roles are implemented, but the MPN data-label taxonomy and applicable classified/PII handling policy are not in the supplied scope. Generic PostgreSQL/UDS source cannot choose that taxonomy.','app-permission-table uds','Obtain the data owner\'s label/category requirement; map tenant/domain attributes where accepted or document supported nonapplicability.','data-label-policy',category='policy/applicability')
decide('206591','Likely covered','Database stderr logs are collected into Vector\'s explicit acknowledged disk buffer and centralized Loki storage, rather than consuming only the database data volume. Final object-store capacity must be sized to the chosen event catalog.','core-vector core-loki app-db-values')
decide('206592 206593','Needs work','UDS provides storage metrics/default cluster alerts, but no candidate audit-specific75-percent threshold and no configured DB-audit-failure route to the required support roles was found. General metrics availability is not an enabled notification.','core-alerts core-vector','Configure the exact audit storage threshold/failure alerts and receivers; share the routing work with other benchmark audit alerts.','audit-alert-routing',category='configuration')
decide('206600 206601','Unclear','The official rules require organization-defined reauthentication/cached-authenticator windows. Native DB accounts exist, but no approved triggers/window is specified. PostgreSQL password sessions are distinct from short-lived browser JWTs.','app-db-identity pg-roles','Define the native DB reauthentication/cached-credential policy and configure/verify it for admin and service paths.',category='policy/session input')
decide('206610 263606','Likely covered','DB software is delivered as an image/release artifact with verified source digests and package provenance; replacement image deployments replace software layers. Approval of trust/signing identities and old PVC/file cleanup must remain in the release procedure.','images app-namespace')
decide('206611 278969','Likely covered','The candidate source builds PostgreSQL18 and the release tooling pins/verifies image identities. That major version is vendor-supported per PostgreSQL\'s supported-version documentation; update timeliness remains an ongoing release-management responsibility.','pg-password images')
decide('206642 263604','Likely covered','Vector continuously collects container stderr and ships it with buffering/acknowledgement to Loki; Grafana centrally queries it. The transport/aggregation path is implemented even though database-audit event selection needs correction.','core-vector core-loki core-grafana pg-logging')
decide('206643','Needs work','The identified native audit/account/backup residuals mean the current candidate cannot be recommended as already configured to all applicable database guidance. This roll-up maps to the existing grouped tasks, not another independent implementation.','app-db-values app-db-role','Close database task groups and retain approved tailoring/inheritance in the component checklist.','compliance-package',category='documentation/configuration')
decide('233495','Needs N/A justification','The official check explicitly exempts an unclassified DB deployment; current MPN is the unclassified/CUI path, separate from the future IL6 authorization effort. Confirm that designation for this package.','uds','Record Austin/data-owner confirmation of MPN classification and accepted N/A; reassess for a classified deployment.',category='applicability')
decide('263602 263603','Needs work','DB-native LOGIN roles are created without expiration or deprovision automation. Keycloak/UDS user disablement does not disable database-native role credentials.','app-db-role app-db-identity','Document account owners, disable/expire human/native accounts as required, and define service-account rotation/offboarding.','database-account-policy',category='configuration/procedure')
decide('263607','Unclear','Application users have individually validated OIDC identity and service DB roles are explicit; however, actual human use/sharing of the bootstrap/admin DB credential cannot be inferred from role-creation code.','app-db-identity authz','Document individual administrator authentication and control use of shared service/break-glass credentials.',category='account ownership')
decide('263608 263609','Unclear','Direct DB service accounts use passwords; the required human-admin MFA may be supplied by an MPN bastion/kubectl path, but that access path and its authentication policy are not in application source. Do not mislabel noninteractive service connections as missing a user MFA prompt.','app-db-identity host','Map each human DBA access path to MPN MFA enforcement or configure the missing control; record service-account applicability separately.',category='host admin access')
decide('263610 263611 263612 263613 263614 263616','Needs work','Native DB passwords are generated/provisioned directly; no compromised-password-list enforcement/update hook, recovery-required-change workflow or interactive password-selection assistance is configured. Keycloak policy does not apply to these roles.','app-db-role app-db-identity','Define native-role account types and enforce/justify each required password/recovery control through approved credential management or DB integration.','database-account-policy',category='configuration/procedure')
decide('263615','Likely covered','PostgreSQL accepts quoted password strings and the provisioning migration safely formats them with %L rather than imposing a restrictive application character/short-length filter. Provider/operational policies must not add unsupported restrictions.','app-db-role pg-password')
decide('263618','Likely covered','Database service is internal to the workload namespace and administrative access is through the separate MPN/UDS management plane; namespace/service identity controls provide logical separation. Native host access topology remains inherited.','core-network app-db-values host')
decide('263621 263622','Likely covered','Database containers use MPN node time; host OS/NTP is inherited rather than a separate NTP daemon inside PostgreSQL. Retain the platform time-control evidence.','host pg-logging')

# More exact application/web and platform rulings discovered in the second sweep.
decide('204708 206350','Needs work','Neither bundled realm nor delivered web config defines a simultaneous-session limit; UDS Core explicitly defaults SSO_SESSION_MAX_PER_USER=0 (unlimited). The official checks do not accept an unlimited/unconfigured limit.','realm core-keycloak app-web','Set approved per-user session/concurrency limits at the effective IdP/gateway; capacity-related connection limits are separate.','session-policy',category='configuration')
decide('204759 204789 204788','Likely covered','UDS Vector defines persistent disk buffers with acknowledgements and continuously offloads to Loki; Grafana supports on-demand query/reduction. This is concrete source evidence for buffering/offload capability, not a request for an unspecified future logging system.','core-vector core-grafana')
